 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<1..100>&cursor=<token>` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <token or null>}`. `limit` defaults to 20. Items are ordered by `id`; pass `next_cursor` unchanged as `cursor` to fetch the next page. The final page has `next_cursor: null`. Invalid pagination parameters return status 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
